SPEC §5 Resolution, §7. One step, returns a Future of the new status, never fails (any error, including a die inside a hook or manifests, becomes phase Error). Order: resolve upstream (controlling coderef > CR spec.upstream > class method > local; "exists" not truthiness; spec.upstream explicit null = local; empty return = local; K8s => (...) and +Class => (...) shortcuts; an object doing Role::Upstream accepted) > enabled > dependencies via resolver (ref "name" or "namespace/name"; resolver returns undef -> Blocked "not found"; dependency healthy false -> Blocked) > check hook (missing prerequisites -> NeedsConfig with message) > local path (healthy -> Running, else manifests -> deploy -> prune -> Pending) > write status. The upstream path (5b) is k5: here only resolution plus a clean hand-off point. Corners from proto (~/dev/proto lib/HI/Comb/Controller.pm _reconcile_one/_prune_orphans/_update_status, inspiration only): (1) enabled undef = auto: SPEC leaves "auto" open; proto used a class flag `optional` (auto = on unless optional) - implement that as an overridable class method and flag it in the report. (2) managedResources must be carried forward in phases that do not deploy (Disabled, Blocked, NeedsConfig, Running), or pruning loses track. (3) Prune only what this Comb recorded AND still carries its comb label; never delete foreign objects. The diff key must not depend on the API version (a v1beta1 -> v1 move must not delete). A failed prune stays in managedResources for the next step. (4) Deploy failing half-way: managedResources = previous union what was applied, phase Error. (5) Conditions: lastTransitionTime changes only when the condition status flips (proto reset it every step). (6) observedGeneration from metadata.generation. (7) Status write via update_status; replace the crd attribute with the returned object; a resourceVersion conflict must not kill reconcile (re-read and retry once, or report) - reconcile still never fails. Without a CR the status lives in memory only.

